  "semantic_scope": "Fixed registered question wording, source integrity, wire identity, admission and response membership; no semantic proof of evidence sufficiency or repair correctness. D089 pins common worker dependency context, public docstring diagnostics and verified owner source context; no automatic ownership override or completion proof. D090 pins native app CLI and model-correct reference pricing; D089 task/repair policies unchanged. D091 adds lossless inline owner encoding and AST/verified artifact-family worker context. Version8 additionally validates guarded Jev Codex worker profile selection; version7 fixed workers. D092 jointly selects actually offered model and effort, with source-pinned public-only observed outcomes. No hidden feedback, learned calibration, automatic fallback, or completed-speed claim. D093: within-family native or Jev judgments select model+effort with the same frozen public outcomes; new native Claude tool-free structured output. App builtins reported separately; external skills/tools disabled. No claim of causal calibration or speed improvement before full completion. Claude recovery changes only native workspace path acceptance for verified macOS /var/folders to /private/var/folders alias, keeping empty workspace and all guards. Prior three records and unstarted fourth condition remain preserved. Claude candidate/worker/task/test/repair/history policies unchanged; paired Claude arms use this same new source phase. New paired Claude attempt after terminal classifier correction: successful generated code text cannot trigger provider error classification. Joint model/effort/history and unknown stop remain unchanged. Prior v12 false denial and unknown decisions preserved; no automatic replay. D094 provisional cold-start selection with null measured rates and one explicit pre-dispatch blocked clarification, preserving uncertain transport and historical results. Single fresh Jev+Claude condition; historical comparisons only. D095: public v5 strengthens response schema imports and configured identifier roundtrip within the93case inventory. Assertion v3 connects revision-bound public failures to current producer/consumer path owners across requirement assignments. Post-hoc public-spec checks, not untouched holdout efficacy. Hidden fixtures/assertions not in prompts. D095 runtime correction: validate current actual round plan hash with fixed implementation ownership independently from initial graph decorations. Preserve v15 harness failure and spending as a separate phase.",
